      "review_notes": "Reviewed the complete supplied excerpt, not the whole meeting package: B53/20 extends the Bell master agreement; eight original bidders are listed but the failed mandatory-stage bidder is unnamed. Bell's $235,000 is forecast annual ongoing-service cost, not a bid or allocated award. B54/20 names electrical and mechanical VOR submissions: 17 category participations from 15 firms, including Ainsworth and Black Creek in both categories. Mechanical Ainsworth and electrical Everbrite are disqualified; the other category participation remains separate. Four winners per category, with Black Creek twice; the $400,000 estimate is an unallocated demand forecast, not a per-vendor award. B55/20 and visible grant attachments contain funding rather than procurement relationships. Benchmark-only reference aliases enumerate the source's printed identifier with its type/No. label or bare shape; they do not infer another identifier, join another document, or change #282 production identity rules. Each normalization is reported alongside the untouched raw response. The resolution uses Ainsworth and Black Creek Mechanical Ltd while the detailed award rationale uses Ainsworth Inc. and Black Creek Mechanical Ltd. These explicitly source-reviewed within-document spellings are accepted by benchmark-only supplier aliases, with every normalization reported. They do not establish external supplier identity or waive category/status distinctions. Post-trial label correction: the detailed rationale explicitly says all eight category winners meet the qualifications and requirements. Their bid statuses are therefore compliant, consistently with D01/D02. The earlier not_stated labels underused that source statement. The frozen pre-trial labels/report are retained, so this correction cannot hide original scores; both human label files remain untouched.",
